kind how-do-i
title How do I make a look on the command line?
intro `vtium-config look add` makes a look in the draft, and `vtium-config look set` sets its font set, size and color scheme. A look changes nothing on screen until a terminal uses it, and vtium-config says so.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console
waits-for audit 10: the command line says nothing when no terminal uses a look

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Press q to quit.
2. Run `vtium-config look add big`.
3. Run `vtium-config look set big --frit mono --size 24`.
at the look is made
check draft look big font-name mono
check said shows "No head uses look big"
